{"questions":[{"id":"p1","kind":"path","question":"When Click parses `--count=3` for the README's `hello` command, in what order does `Command.parse_args` run the three parameters through `handle_parse_result`, and what rule produces that order?","key":"The order is [the automatic help option (name `_click_default_help`), `count`, `name`]. `iter_params_for_processing` sorts the declaration order with key `(not is_eager, invocation_index)`: the help option is `is_eager=True` so it sorts first; `count` is not eager but appears in the parser's invocation order at index 0, while `name` never appeared on the command line so its index is `float('inf')`, putting `count` before `name`.","lines":["src/click/core.py:168-192","src/click/core.py:1392-1400"],"check":"import click
from click.core import iter_params_for_processing

@click.command()
@click.option('--count', default=1, help='Number of greetings.')
@click.option('--name', prompt='Your name', help='The person to greet.')
def hello(count, name):
    pass

ctx = click.Context(hello, info_name='hello')
params = hello.get_params(ctx)
count = [p for p in params if p.name == 'count'][0]
order = iter_params_for_processing([count], params)
assert [p.name for p in order] == ['_click_default_help', 'count', 'name'], [p.name for p in order]
help_opt = hello.get_help_option(ctx)
assert help_opt.is_eager is True
assert count.is_eager is False
"},{"id":"p2","kind":"path","question":"What exactly does the low-level option parser return for the token `--count=3` (the `opts` mapping, leftover args, and invocation order), before any type conversion happens?","key":"`_OptionParser.parse_args(['--count=3'])` returns `({'count': '3'}, [], [<Option count>])`: the value is still the string `'3'` (the `=` is split off by `_process_opts` and consumed by `_match_long_opt`/`_get_value_from_state`), there are no leftover args, and the order list contains only the `count` Option object. Conversion to the int 3 happens later in `Parameter.type_cast_value`.","lines":["src/click/parser.py:298-314","src/click/parser.py:470-500","src/click/core.py:1396-1397"],"check":"import click

