"},{"id":"p3","kind":"path","question":"For this run, what `ParameterSource` does the context record for `count`, for `name`, and for the automatic help option, and why does `name` get that source?","key":"`count` -> `ParameterSource.COMMANDLINE` (the parser produced a value), `name` -> `ParameterSource.PROMPT`, and `_click_default_help` -> `ParameterSource.DEFAULT`. `name` is PROMPT because `Option.consume_value` found no command-line value, no envvar and no default-map entry (source was DEFAULT, i.e. >= DEFAULT_MAP), the option has `prompt='Your name'` with `prompt_required=True`, and parsing is not resilient, so it calls `prompt_for_value` and overwrites the source with PROMPT; the value returned is the string 'Click'.","lines":["src/click/core.py:3769-3780","src/click/core.py:2586-2632","src/click/core.py:2857-2863"],"check":"import click
from click.core import ParameterSource
from click.testing import CliRunner

seen = {}

@click.command()
@click.option('--count', default=1)
@click.option('--name', prompt='Your name')
@click.pass_context
