"},{"id":"p4","kind":"path","question":"Neither option declares a `type`. What ParamType ends up on `--count` and on `--name`, where does it come from, and what Python value does the callback receive for `count`?","key":"`--count` gets `click.INT` (an `IntParamType`, `name == 'integer'`), inferred by `types.convert_type(None, default)` from the default value `1` in `Parameter.__init__`. `--name` has no default, so `convert_type(None, UNSET)` falls through to `click.STRING` (`StringParamType`). The callback receives `count` as the int `3` (converted from the parser's string `'3'`) and `name` as the str `'Click'`.","lines":["src/click/core.py:2389","src/click/types.py:1356-1397","src/click/core.py:2657-2660"],"check":"import click
