"},{"id":"p6","kind":"path","question":"The trace shows a third parameter being created during parsing. Under what name is the automatic `--help` option stored, is it in `hello.params`, and which keys end up in `ctx.params`?","key":"`Command.get_help_option` lazily builds it via the `help_option` decorator with the reserved storage name `_HELP_OPTION_STORAGE_NAME = '_click_default_help'`, then pops it off `self.params` and caches it in `self._help_option`, so it is not part of `hello.params` (it is only appended by `get_params`). It has `opts == ['--help']`, `expose_value=False` and `is_eager=True`, so it never writes to `ctx.params`; `ctx.params` holds exactly `{'count', 'name'}`.","lines":["src/click/core.py:59-61","src/click/core.py:1218-1250","src/click/core.py:2909-2912"],"check":"import click
