"},{"id":"g3","kind":"general","question":"What does `Command.get_params` check about parameter names and option spellings, when do those checks run, and what happens when a check trips?","key":"Inside an `if __debug__:` block (so the checks vanish under `python -O`), `get_params` builds the full list (declared params plus the help option) and emits `warnings.warn(..., stacklevel=3)` — a `UserWarning`, not an error — for: (1) any option spelling appearing in more than one parameter ("The parameter X is used more than once..."), (2) a user parameter sharing the storage name of the automatic help option ("The name ... is reserved for the automatic help option"), and (3) a name shared between an `Argument` and another parameter ("... will overwrite each other's value during parsing"). Options sharing a name with each other are allowed on purpose (feature switches) and are not warned about. The warnings are re-emitted every time `get_params` is called, and parsing continues regardless.","lines":["src/click/core.py:1128-1182"],"check":"import warnings
